# Maintainer scratch space. Untracked by convention since it was created; this makes that
# explicit, because convention alone does not stop `git add -A`. It did not: one `git add -A
# backend scratchpad` swept 428 files of working notes, mutation harnesses and drill output
# into a public PR, where CI caught it only because the shellcheck job lints "every tracked
# script" and suddenly had eighty more.
#
# Nothing here has ever been tracked, so ignoring it orphans nothing. Note that CLAUDE.md and
# the arc handoffs cite paths under this directory (scratchpad/HANDOFF-*.md, build specs) —
# those references are to files on a maintainer's disk, not to repo content, and that is the
# arrangement being made explicit rather than changed.
scratchpad/
